[82.128197, "o", "b"]
[82.618136, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[82.666764, "o", "The access token Amazon Cognito gives bob after sign-in to the helpdesk-web app.\r\nA real one is a signed JWT: three base64 parts (header.claims.signature). These are its claims:\r\n\r\n  iss        https://cognito-idp.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/us-east-1_EXAMPLE1   issuer: who signed it (AnyCompany's Cognito user pool)\r\n  sub        sub-bob                                                          subject: the user's fixed ID in that pool\r\n  client_id  7helpdeskweb0example0client                                      which app asked for the token\r\n  token_use  access                                                           an access token, for calling things\r\n  scope      openid profile                                                   what the token allows\r\n  username   bob                                                              the user name, also a claim\r\n\r\nThe browser sends it as: Authorization: Bearer <token>. Anyone who checks it reads these claims.\r\n"]
[82.674751, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m14\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m14\u001b[00m$ "]
