[168.473163, "o", "d"]
[168.945719, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[168.995816, "o", "Gateway tsg-helpdesk-gw (hardened): MCP endpoint, inbound CUSTOM_JWT\r\n\r\n  target HelpdeskTools = Lambda function tsg-helpdesk-tools, outbound credential GATEWAY_IAM_ROLE\r\n  tools/list shows the agent these tools (target___tool):\r\n    HelpdeskTools___search_kb    (query)  Search the IT knowledge base\r\n    HelpdeskTools___reset_mfa    (target_username, caller_username)  Reset a user's MFA device\r\n    HelpdeskTools___send_email   (to, subject, body, caller_username)  Send an email for the signed-in user\r\n\r\n  tools/call reset_mfa -> the gateway invokes the Lambda with its own role, tsg-gateway-role. The Lambda gets:\r\n    event   {\"target_username\": \"...\", \"caller_username\": \"...\"}       the tool input, nothing else\r\n    context gateway ID, target ID, tool name, request IDs               nothing about the end user\r\n\r\n=> the tools Lambda can't tell Bob from Alice. The check has to happen before it: in the gateway's policy.\r\n"]
[169.003535, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m14\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m14\u001b[00m$ "]
